<%# locals: (celebrate:, child:) -%>
<%#
  The end of the day, in the box the questions were in: the child's name, and no sentence. The
  stars are the progress row above, which is full by definition at this point and grows into
  the celebration rather than being joined by a second row of its own. It is rendered under the
  verdict or the correction exactly as the next card is, so whatever lifts one of those is what
  reveals it.
%>

<%= tag.div class: "done", data: { screen: "done", controller: ("done" if celebrate) } do %>
  <div class="done-name"><%= child.name %></div>
<% end %>
